---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteBase } from "../utils/site.js";
import latestRun from "../../../benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-multi-tool-8ffc709.json";
import focusedRun from "../../../benchmarks/results/miniwob-targeted-browser-fixes-8490bd7.json";
import cpuDecisionRun from "../../../benchmarks/results/decision-cases-independent-ryzen5600h-cpu-smoke.json";
import dmlDecisionRun from "../../../benchmarks/results/decision-cases-independent-ryzen5600h-dml-smoke.json";

const episodeCount = latestRun.episodeCount;
const successCount = latestRun.successCount;
const failureCount = episodeCount - successCount;
const successPercent = Math.round(latestRun.taskSuccessRate * 100);
const environment = latestRun.rawRecords[0];
const commitUrl = `https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/commit/${latestRun.suite.agentDecisionKitCommit}`;
const rawRunUrl = "https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-multi-tool-8ffc709.json";
const decisionRows = [
  { device: "CPU", report: cpuDecisionRun },
  { device: "DirectML requested", report: dmlDecisionRun },
].map(({ device, report }) => {
  const reliability = report.confidenceReliability.find((item) => item.outcome === "predicted choice/yes-no correctness");
  return {
    device,
    firstCall: report.latencyMs.firstCallIncludingInitialization,
    p50: report.latencyMs.withinProcessSteadyState.p50,
    p95: report.latencyMs.withinProcessSteadyState.p95,
    warmCount: report.latencyMs.withinProcessSteadyState.sampleCount,
    choiceCorrect: Math.round(report.byQuestionType.choice.accuracy * report.byQuestionType.choice.sampleCount),
    choiceTotal: report.byQuestionType.choice.sampleCount,
    yesNoCorrect: Math.round(report.byQuestionType.noul.accuracy * report.byQuestionType.noul.sampleCount),
    yesNoTotal: report.byQuestionType.noul.sampleCount,
    choiceBrier: report.byQuestionType.choice.meanBrierScore,
    yesNoBrier: report.byQuestionType.noul.meanBrierScore,
    scoreMae: report.byQuestionType.score.meanAbsoluteError,
    ece: reliability?.expectedCalibrationError ?? null,
    eceCount: reliability?.sampleCount ?? 0,
  };
});
---

<BaseLayout title="Real Browser Automation Benchmarks | Agent Decision Kit" description="Reproducible Playwright and BrowserGym MiniWoB results for Agent Decision Kit, with task success, latency, environment details, and raw episodes." canonicalPath="benchmarks/">
  <main class="page">
    <header class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">MEASURED RUNS · RAW EPISODES INCLUDED</p>
      <h1>Browser automation<br /><span>with the limits in view.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Real BrowserGym MiniWoB runs from this repository. Each report keeps task success, latency, failures, and the environment together so a small smoke run stays a small claim.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="latest" aria-labelledby="latest-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">LATEST MULTI-TOOL INTEGRATION</p>
        <h2 id="latest-title">{successCount} of {episodeCount} tasks succeeded.</h2>
        <p>The bounded harness extracted explicit targets from synthetic task instructions, used <code>browser_copy_field</code> and <code>browser_set_checkboxes</code> for local form workflows, and exercised <code>browser_set_range</code> on keyboard-operated sliders. Each Submit action still received a separate local-only synthetic approval. This rerun on commit {latestRun.suite.agentDecisionKitCommit.slice(0, 7)} reproduced 23/26 successes; the same three task goals remain unmet. The two visual-only pages received local image descriptions but no browser action. This measures tool integration, not an autonomous coding-agent score.</p>
        <p class="comparison-note">Task success requires a raw MiniWoB reward of at least 1.0; positive partial rewards count as failures. This avoids BrowserGym 0.14.3's partial-reward-to-success conversion documented in <a href="https://github.com/ServiceNow/BrowserGym/issues/392">upstream issue 392</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="success-chart">
        <div class="bar" role="img" aria-label={`${successCount} tasks succeeded and ${failureCount} tasks did not succeed, out of ${episodeCount}`}>
          <span class="passed" style={`width:${successPercent}%`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="failed" style={`width:${100 - successPercent}%`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <span><i class="legend passed-key"></i>{successCount} succeeded</span>
          <span><i class="legend failed-key"></i>{failureCount} did not reach the task goal</span>
          <span>0 harness timeouts</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="metrics-grid">
        <article class="metric"><p class="eyebrow">TASK SUCCESS</p><strong>{successCount}/{episodeCount}</strong><span>{successPercent}% on this curated set</span></article>
        <article class="metric"><p class="eyebrow">BROWSER LOOP P50</p><strong>{(latestRun.agentActionLatencyMs.p50 / 1000).toFixed(2)}s</strong><span>Includes tool actions and inspection</span></article>
        <article class="metric"><p class="eyebrow">BROWSER LOOP P95</p><strong>{(latestRun.agentActionLatencyMs.p95 / 1000).toFixed(1)}s</strong><span>Two local vision descriptions drive the slow tail</span></article>
        <article class="metric"><p class="eyebrow">DECISION CALL P95</p><strong>{latestRun.decisionCallLatencyMs.p95}ms</strong><span>Cold call in a new Node process per task</span></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="conditions" aria-labelledby="conditions-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">REPRODUCTION DETAILS</p>
        <h2 id="conditions-title">A CPU run with a fixed task set.</h2>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Agent Decision Kit</dt><dd><a href={commitUrl}>{latestRun.suite.agentDecisionKitCommit.slice(0, 7)}</a></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Benchmark</dt><dd>BrowserGym MiniWoB 0.14.3</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Browser and runtimes</dt><dd>{environment.browserVersion} · Node {environment.nodeVersion} · Python {environment.pythonVersion} · Playwright Python {environment.playwrightPythonVersion} / Node {environment.playwrightNodeVersion}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Machine</dt><dd>{environment.operatingSystem} · {environment.cpuModel}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Runner image</dt><dd>{environment.containerImage} · {environment.containerImageId.slice(0, 19)}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Task set</dt><dd>26 curated MiniWoB tasks · seed 7 · eight actions per task</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Model path</dt><dd>Local semantic model and CPU visual descriptions; no remote decision provider</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <b>How to read the latency</b>
        <p>Every task starts a fresh Node bridge. Four timed decision calls had p50 {latestRun.decisionCallLatencyMs.p50} ms / p95 {latestRun.decisionCallLatencyMs.p95} ms. This run does not establish warm throughput or the consumer-GPU target.</p>
        <p>Two visual-only pages used local image description on CPU and took 25.8 s and 31.5 s; neither received a browser action. The text and OCR action tools were not exercised in this run.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={rawRunUrl}>Inspect the summary and all raw episodes ↗</a>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="decision-runs" aria-labelledby="decision-runs-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL DECISION DEVICE CHECK</p>
      <h2 id="decision-runs-title">CPU was faster on this small model.</h2>
      <p class="comparison-note">Both runs used the same 30 project-specific labels on one Windows 10 Ryzen 5 5600H laptop with an operator-reported GeForce GTX 1650 (4 GB). The model-cache directory existed before each run, but cached files were not individually checked. A DirectML device was requested for the GPU row; ONNX Runtime's per-node execution and CPU fallback were not inspected.</p>
      <div class="decision-table-wrap">
        <table>
          <caption>One paired run · 29 within-process calls after initialization · labels are not held out</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Requested device</th><th scope="col">First call</th><th scope="col">Warm p50 / p95</th><th scope="col">Choice</th><th scope="col">Yes/no</th><th scope="col">Score MAE</th><th scope="col">Brier: Choice / yes-no</th><th scope="col">ECE (n=20)</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {decisionRows.map((row) => <tr>
              <th scope="row">{row.device}</th>
              <td>{row.firstCall} ms</td>
              <td>{row.p50} / {row.p95} ms (n={row.warmCount})</td>
              <td>{row.choiceCorrect}/{row.choiceTotal}</td>
              <td>{row.yesNoCorrect}/{row.yesNoTotal}</td>
              <td>{row.scoreMae.toFixed(3)}</td>
              <td>{row.choiceBrier.toFixed(3)} / {row.yesNoBrier.toFixed(3)}</td>
              <td>{row.ece?.toFixed(3) ?? "not reported"}</td>
            </tr>)}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="comparison-note">The GPU request was slower in this paired run: warm p95 was 132 ms versus 17 ms on CPU. Both measured p95 values are below 500 ms here, but this small non-held-out sample does not establish the target or a general speed guarantee. Confidence estimates remain uncalibrated; ECE is descriptive only.</p>
      <div class="decision-raw-links"><a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/decision-cases-independent-ryzen5600h-cpu-smoke.json">CPU raw data ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/decision-cases-independent-ryzen5600h-dml-smoke.json">DirectML-request raw data ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/fixtures/decision-cases-independent.jsonl">30 labeled examples ↗</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="other-runs" aria-labelledby="other-runs-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">OTHER RECORDED RUNS</p>
      <h2 id="other-runs-title">Different runs answer different questions.</h2>
      <div class="run-list">
        <article>
          <div><strong>22/26</strong><span>Intermediate pointer run</span></div>
          <p>The exact-sender email flow passed, while duplicate nested menu targets caused a regression. The later pointer-wrapper fix restored that menu task; the two visual-only tasks and <code>read-table-2</code> still failed.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-multi-tool-00b7b13.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>20/26</strong><span>Earlier same-task run</span></div>
          <p>Same 26 tasks, seed, and action cap as the latest run, before local field-copy and multi-checkbox tools. Two outcomes changed from failure to success in the later run; this paired observation does not establish a general quality or speed improvement.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-multi-tool-60bec66.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>19/26</strong><span>Prior multi-tool baseline</span></div>
          <p>The same task set before support for MiniWoB's keyboard-operated sliders. It did not call <code>browser_set_range</code>; <code>use-slider-2</code> was the only task outcome that changed in the later run.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-multi-tool-b901f05.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>{focusedRun.successCount}/{focusedRun.episodeCount}</strong><span>Focused browser regressions</span></div>
          <p>Six previously troublesome MiniWoB cases on Linux CPU. Browser action-loop p50 258 ms / p95 721 ms, with zero semantic model calls. This is a targeted regression set, not a general success estimate.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-targeted-browser-fixes-8490bd7.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>8/8</strong><span>Focused MiniWoB smoke</span></div>
          <p>Eight curated tasks on Linux CPU. Browser action-loop p50 305 ms / p95 699 ms. One integration run; not a general success estimate.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-pointer-fastpath-diagnostic-rerun-smoke.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>3/3</strong><span>Full-reward tool smoke</span></div>
          <p>Three explicitly selected tasks reached raw reward 1.0. The bounded, deterministic harness exercised checkbox batching, local field copy, and keyboard sliders. Browser-loop p50 927 ms / p95 1,005 ms; there were no semantic model calls. Synthetic submit approvals were limited to the local benchmark page. This is a small integration check, not a representative success estimate.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-post-reward-fix-smoke.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div><strong>3/26</strong><span>Decision/action only</span></div>
          <p>A broader task mix that repeatedly called the decision/action tool without orchestrating form fills, native select options, or visual inspection.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/miniwob-expanded-smoke-suite.json">Raw run ↗</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="comparison-note">The latest and prior 26-task runs share a task set, seed, and action cap, but each is one CPU integration observation on a changing toolchain; neither establishes general browser quality or speed. Other counts use different task sets. No Jev parity comparison has been run. The original multi-site WebArena and VisualWebArena suites have no results; a separate single-site WebArena Verified smoke reached only partial reward 0.5, not full task success.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/README.md">Read the full protocol and reproduction commands →</a>
    </section>

    <section class="prerequisites" aria-labelledby="prerequisites-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">BROADER BROWSERGYM SETUPS</p>
      <h2 id="prerequisites-title">WebArena scores need running benchmark sites.</h2>
      <p class="prerequisite-lead">Installing BrowserGym alone does not provide the original WebArena or VisualWebArena sites. Their integrations need several configured domains; those full suites have no result here. A separate one-site WebArena Verified navigation smoke is recorded below as a partial integration check.</p>
      <div class="setup-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>WebArena</h3>
          <p>Requires URLs for the shopping site and admin, Reddit, GitLab, Wikipedia, map, and homepage.</p>
          <code>WA_SHOPPING · WA_REDDIT · WA_GITLAB · WA_WIKIPEDIA · WA_MAP · WA_HOMEPAGE</code>
          <a href="https://github.com/ServiceNow/BrowserGym/blob/main/browsergym/webarena/README.md">BrowserGym WebArena setup ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>VisualWebArena</h3>
          <p>Requires separate classifieds, shopping, Reddit, Wikipedia, and homepage URLs.</p>
          <code>VWA_CLASSIFIEDS · VWA_SHOPPING · VWA_REDDIT · VWA_WIKIPEDIA · VWA_HOMEPAGE</code>
          <a href="https://github.com/ServiceNow/BrowserGym/blob/main/browsergym/visualwebarena/README.md">BrowserGym VisualWebArena setup ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>WebArena Verified · one site</h3>
          <p>One read-only navigation smoke received partial reward 0.5 and did not complete the task. The action loop guard stopped repeated menu toggles after five browser actions.</p>
          <code>BrowserGym 0.14.3 · shopping_admin · 1 task · 0/1 full successes</code>
          <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/webarena-verified-shopping-admin-157-loop-guard.json">Raw partial result ↗</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="comparison-note">The upstream WebArena guide notes that some fuzzy-match evaluations call a hosted GPT-4 judge. The default Agent Decision Kit benchmark path stays local and does not enable paid judging. See the <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/README.md#webarena-and-visualwebarena-prerequisites">prerequisites and evaluator policy</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
